WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.190
Here is the HOA platform's public sample
experience, built

2
00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:08.690
by Catalyst Innovations. The communities
and information in this demonstration

3
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.870
are fictional. We will follow a resident
request from the first description

4
00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:16.850
to the final review. Start by giving the
request a clear title.

5
00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:21.690
Then describe what needs attention, so the
community team has useful context

6
00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:26.150
from the beginning. In this example, the
resident is reporting a problem with

7
00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:30.610
path lighting. Next, the form explains
what supporting information could

8
00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:32.610
help the team understand the request.

9
00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:36.790
Clear guidance at this stage can make the
handoff easier and reduce the need

10
00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:40.610
to chase missing details. Continue to the
review screen.

11
00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:44.710
The resident can check the information
before sending it, and go back if

12
00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:48.670
something needs changing. We are stopping
here without submitting a request.

13
00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:52.230
Sending a request does not approve the
work or reserve a date.

14
00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:56.550
This workflow gives the resident a clear
starting point and the community team

15
00:00:56.560 --> 00:01:00.590
a more structured handoff. Talk with
Catalyst about simplifying the everyday

16
00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:01.970
work in your community.

